  "notes": ["HOT notes for this cruise: 10-30 dbar averages used due to transient influence of heavy rainfall on 5 dbar sample (code q).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No DIC data in upper 30 dbar; used value from 34.0 dbar (code e). No TA data in upper 30 dbar; used value from 51.3 dbar (code f).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No DIC or TA data in upper 30 dbar; used values from 34.9 dbar (code m).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No DIC or TA data in upper 30 dbar; used values from 44.9 dbar (code n).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No DIC, TA or pH sampling occurred (code p).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No DIC, TA or pH sampling occurred in upper 200 dbar (code o).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No HOT DIC data; used Keeling DIC (code a).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No HOT DIC data; used Keeling DIC (code a). No HOT TA data; used Keeling TA (code b).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No HOT DIC data; used Keeling DIC (code a). No HOT TA data; used Keeling TA (code b). Used temp and sal data from downcast before cable broke (code g). No phos data; assumed 0.07 (code h). No sil data; assumed 1.04 (code i). Rosette lost; samples collected with Go-flo bottle on Kevlar line (code j).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No HOT TA data; used Keeling TA (code b).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No TA data; assumed nTA of 2303.2 (code d).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No phos data; assumed 0.07 (code h).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No rosette; samples collected with Niskin bottles on Kevlar line (code l).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No sampling occurred (code k).", "HOT notes for this cruise: No sil data; assumed 1.04 (code i)."],
